esp32s31-hosted: a coexistence control message, and no per-IRQ mask dance

Cumulative diff from the 6.12 BSP baseline (the linux-esp32-s31 submodule)
to the current 7.1 state of the hosted transport driver, in the same form
as 0023 for the display stack.

Coexistence: Bluetooth's host stack is on Linux, so hart0's radio
arbiter could never learn that A2DP was streaming, and a Wi-Fi download
starved the stream to 7-20 ACL packets/s (btmon; completions still
tracked, so the controller was completing fewer packets over the air,
not losing credits). S31_HOSTED_IOC_COEX on /dev/esps0 carries a
S31_HOSTED_CTRL_COEX_SET message to hart0, which applies
esp_coex_status_bit_set/clear, esp_coex_preference_set and
coex_schm_interval_set. s31-a2dp sets ESP_COEX_BT_ST_A2DP_STREAMING on
transport acquire: measured, the same 5.9 MB download while streaming
goes from 2.8 s late with 83 stalls to 0-7 ms late with none, at ~250
instead of ~328 KB/s of Wi-Fi.

Also drops the disable_irq_nosync()/enable_irq() pair around NAPI - the
doorbell ack is the mask, and a doorbell during a scheduled poll just
finds napi_schedule_prep() false. Measured no faster, kept because it
is the standard shape and one lock fewer per interrupt.

